      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes Requested**\n\nIf `CONFIG_HAVE_RTS5817MAA_PRIVATE_DRIVER` is disabled, `rts5817maa_sensor_get_hwid` is skipped, meaning `ret` and `sensor_id` remain `0`. The function then blindly assigns `sensor_info-\u003emodel_id \u003d sensor_id;`, which incorrectly overwrites the default `model_id` of `1` (from the macro) with `0`.\n\nPlease enclose the error checking and assignment inside the `IS_ENABLED` block so the default values are preserved when the private driver is disabled:\n\n```c\n\tif (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_HAVE_RTS5817MAA_PRIVATE_DRIVER)) {\n\t\tret \u003d rts5817maa_sensor_get_hwid(\u0026sensor_id);\n\t\tif (ret) {\n\t\t\tLOG_ERR(\"Failed to get sensor hwid: %d\", ret);\n\t\t\treturn -EINVAL;\n\t\t}\n\t\tsensor_info-\u003emodel_id \u003d sensor_id;\n\t}\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/6f389ceb-7f03-4dd0-925a-d102091adef7)",
