      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes Requested**\n\nThe `dev` argument passed to the GPIO interrupt callback is the GPIO port device, not the fingerprint sensor device. By calling `data-\u003ecallback(dev);`, the fingerprint core will receive the GPIO port device pointer instead of the fingerprint device pointer, which will lead to memory corruption or crashes when it attempts to use it.\n\nPlease pass `data-\u003edev` to the callback instead:\n\n```c\nstatic void rts5817maa_irq(const struct device *dev, struct gpio_callback *cb,\n\t\t       uint32_t pins)\n{\n\tstruct rts5817maa_data *data \u003d CONTAINER_OF(cb, struct rts5817maa_data, irq_cb);\n\n\trts5817maa_disable_irq(data-\u003edev);\n\n\tif (data-\u003ecallback !\u003d NULL) {\n\t\tdata-\u003ecallback(data-\u003edev);\n\t}\n}\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/6f389ceb-7f03-4dd0-925a-d102091adef7)",
